        <div class="col-md-12 portfolio-custom text-center">
            <h4 class="text-white">Art</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="text-orange">
            <div class="col-sm-12 portfolio-custom text-left">
                <p>Most of the art was created using a Fortnite-style grid system standard in mind. All building blocks, piping variants, and doodads, were made to be all modular and easy to fit on a 256 unit grid.</p>
                <p>I could make assets and hand them off with, supporting documentation to use the grid, to the dedicated level designer for him to easily place around the map.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-12 portfolio-custom text-left">
                <p>One of the challenges I faced was halfway through the time left, one my teammates had an awesome idea on how the black hole would consume the level, that would require me to remake all the building blocks, and I happily obliged and I am so happy I did cause the end result was well worth the time refactoring.</p>
            </div>
        </div>


